DESCRIPTION:Event by Corning's Gaffer District\nMarket Street\, Corning NY
 \nDuration: 2 days\nPublic\nHarvest 2026\nCelebrate the flavors\, sights\,
  and spirit of fall in Downtown Corning during Harvest!\nJoin us for two d
 ays of seasonal fun as Market Street comes alive with local vendors\, shop
 ping\, dining\, live entertainment\, and festive fall activities. Whether 
 you're looking for unique handmade goods\, delicious food\, or a great way
  to spend the day with family and friends\, Harvest is the perfect way to 
 welcome the autumn season in the Crystal City.\nEvent Hours\nFriday\, Sept
 ember 18: 12:00 PM – 8:00 PM\nSaturday\, September 19: 11:00 AM – 7:00
  PM\nMark your calendars and stay tuned—more information is coming soon
 \, including our vendor lineup\, live music schedule\, featured activities
 \, and more!\nHARVEST 2026 ACTIVITIES\nFRIDAY\, SEPTEMBER 18\nCentennial S
 culpture\n2:30 - 4:00 PM — Plein Air Watercolo. r Workshop with Bridget 
 Bossart van Otterloo (Friday Tickets Here)\nKid Zone\n12:00 - 8:00 PM — 
 Kid Zone Games & Crafts\n2:00 - 8:00 PM — Balloons by Mandy\n5:00 - 7:00
  PM — Autumn-Themed Glass Mosaic Tile Making with Aubergine Glass\nChest
 nut Street Park\n3:00 - 7:00 PM — Pony Rides\n3:00 - 7:00 PM — Highlan
 d Cow Experience\n5:00 - 8:00 PM — Magic with Collin Ward (sponsored by 
 Leaf Filter)\nPedestrian Bridge\n5:00–8:00 PM — Paint & Sip with Kylen
 e Kiah of Pop & Paint (Tickets Here)\nSATURDAY\, SEPTEMBER 19\nPine Street
 \n1:30 - 3:00 PM — Plein Air Watercolor Workshop with Bridget Bossart va
 n Otterloo (Saturday Tickets Here)\nBlock 1\n1:00 - 5:00 PM — Horse & Wa
 gon Rides\nKid Zone\n12:00 - 7:00 PM — Kid Zone Games & Crafts\n12:00 - 
 2:00 & 3:00 - 5:00 PM — Autumn-Themed Glass Mosaic Tiles by Aubergine Gl
 ass\n11:00 AM - 7:00 PM — Face Painting & Glitter Tattoos by Painted Lov
 e\nBlock 4\n11:00 AM - 6:00 PM — Magic with Collin Ward\n11:00 AM - 7:00
  PM - YMCA Kid Zone\nMusic Lineup\nFRIDAY\, SEPTEMBER 18\nCenterway Square
 \n12:00 - 1:30 PM — Simply Ira\n2:00 - 3:30 PM — Mystic Twangers\n4:00
  - 5:30 PM — Peyton Clark\n6:00 - 8:00 PM — Justin Raynor\nMusic - Blo
 ck 2 (Between Cedar Street & Pine Street\n12:30 - 2:30 PM — Taylor Hurd
 \n3:00 - 4:30 PM — Silver Linings Trio\n5:00 - 7:00 PM — One Eared Cat
 \nGaffer District Stage - Block 5 (Between Chestnut Street & Tarantelli La
 ne)\n12:00 - 2:00 PM — Gerard Burke\n4:00 - 7:00 PM — JOGO\nSATURDAY\,
  SEPTEMBER 19\nCenterway Square\n12:00 - 2:00 PM — Pat Kane Music & Squa
 re Dancing\n3:00 - 5:00 PM — Taylor Hurd\n5:30 - 7:30 PM — Sing Trece
 \nMusic - Block 2 (Between Cedar Street & Pine Street)\n12:00 - 2:00 PM 
 — JOGO\n3:00 - 4:30 PM — Silver Linings Trio\nGaffer District Stage - 
 Block 5 (Between Chestnut Street & Tarantelli Lane)\n11:00 AM - 12:30 PM 
 — One Eared Cat\n1:00 - 3:00 PM — Annie Ol' Thyme\n4:00 - 7:00 PM — 
 Simply Ira\nWe can't wait to celebrate the season with you in Downtown Cor
 ning! A huge Thank you to our sponsor\, Williams Toyota!\n\nSource: FLXcal
 endar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78466291/20260918120000
