DESCRIPTION:Lil Rockwell | Stroller Walk: Día de los Muertos\nThursday\, 
 October 1\, 2026\n10:00 am - 11:00 am\nLocation: Nonnie Hood PRC\nFree for
  children and their caregivers | No registration required\nLocation: Meet 
 at Nonnie Hood PRC and walk to the KIDS ROCKWELL Art Lab\nMeet us at the P
 RC for a fun walk down Market Street to the Art Lab! See the brand-new All
 ey Art mural at the Southeast Steuben County Library\, and the colorful of
 renda in the window of the Art Lab. Enjoy a story with Miss Sue and learn 
 about Día de los Muertos! Stay after the program to explore the self-guid
 ed activities in the Art Lab and exciting exhibitions at The Rockwell Muse
 um.\nLil Rockwell creates opportunities to explore art-viewing and artmaki
 ng for our littlest visitors and their caregivers. During different months
 \, you’ll find either an art class suitable for children 18 mo-5 years\;
  a story hour for children of all ages\; or a stroller walk\, where even i
 nfants can participate! Lil Rockwell occurs on the first Thursday of every
  month except for September. This program is designed to engage your littl
 e ones through art exploration\; and for the grown-ups–we have coffee!\n
 Rain Date: Friday\, October 2\, 10 a.m.- 11 a.m.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - 
 https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78466375/20261001100000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78466375/20261001100000
