BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Trio Espressivo!
DTSTART:20261009T233000Z
DTEND:20261010T035959Z
DTSTAMP:20260919T130751Z
UID:3182b7116283f0f93b860f805a917922452b54b4@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music,Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Event by The Orchestra of the Southern Finger Lakes\nNorth Pre
 sbyterian Church\n921 College Ave\, Elmira\, NY\nPublic\nTravel through a 
 century of musical change featuring pianist Grace Cox\, violinist Oliver K
 riska\, and cellist Eric Johnson.\nThe ensemble pairs some of the most bel
 oved works in the piano trio repertoire with lesser-known pieces that dese
 rve a place in the spotlight. Arrive early for a complimentary tasting fro
 m HoneyBeeMade!\nThe program spans from the expressive Romanticism of Céc
 ile Chaminade and Felix Mendelssohn to the rhythmic vitality of Bohuslav M
 artinů’s Bergerettes\, written approximately a century later. Though th
 ese composers worked in different eras\, their music shares structures\, i
 deas and musical conversations that reveal how classical traditions endure
  even as composers take them in exciting new directions.\nThroughout the e
 vening\, the musicians will introduce the works and offer insight into the
 ir history\, structure and composers\, inviting audiences to listen more c
 losely and discover connections they may not expect. Presented in the inti
 mate\, relaxed tradition of the Musicians’ Choice Chamber Music Series\,
  the concert offers an engaging introduction for newcomers and a fresh per
 spective for longtime chamber music listeners.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - ht
 tps://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78466307/20261009193000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78466307/20261009193000
END:VEVENT
