BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fireside Chat w/ local author Carey Crooker
DTSTART:20261019T220000Z
DTEND:20261019T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260919T130751Z
UID:43a9c4da7b7d49ea5fe57e33f1801c0359da86d7@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Literature
DESCRIPTION:Event by Southeast Steuben County Library and Carey Crooker Wr
 ites\n300 Nasser Civic Center Plaza\, Corning\, NY\nDuration: 1 hr\nPublic
 \nJoin us and local author Carey Crooker as she introduces her first book
 \, "Second Place."\nThe book tells the story of Rachel\, a married mother 
 of four. When her marriage begins unraveling and her past resurfaces\, Rac
 hel finds herself caught between brothers Luke and John. She thinks going 
 back to her hometown will help her gain some clarity\, but it only complic
 ates things and no matter who she picks\, one of them will end up hurt.\nA
 bout the author: Carey Crooker is a professional photographer\, a mom\, an
 d now a published author who lives in Addison\, NY. She loves small-town l
 ife\, eating ice cream\, nail-biter indoor soccer tournaments\, and findin
 g humor in parenting. Second Place is her first novel and is available on 
 Amazon. Second Place is a clean romance told in alternating timelines with
  short chapters that make it hard to put down.\nYou can follow "Carey Croo
 ker Writes" on Facebook for updates on the sequel: bit.ly/CareyCrookerFB\n
 \nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78466400/2
 0261019180000
GEO:42.142288;-77.047119
LOCATION:Southeast Steuben County Library\, 300 Nasser Civic Center Plaza
 \, Corning\, New York\, Corning\, New York\, 14830\, United States
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78466400/20261019180000
