BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening | Everlasting (a film on Cornelius 'Pepsi' Lyon by 
 Caleb Kaufman)
DTSTART:20261022T220000Z
DTEND:20261022T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260919T130751Z
UID:e0336fe67776ef674ae8590b4962c13f852275d0@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film,Art
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a one-night-only screening of Everlasting\, a docu
 mentary film by director Caleb Kaufman that chronicles the life and work o
 f Cornelius "Pepsi" Lyon.\nFor more than 15 years\, Pepsi has been an acti
 ve member of the Corning Museum of Glass and The Studio's community\; he's
  taken glassmaking classes\, became a regular hot shop renter\, and met th
 e love of his life at The Studio. Pepsi has also spent decades creating wh
 at is believed to be the largest privately built sculpture garden in North
  America. Everlasting beautifully captures his artistic journey\, this ext
 raordinary project\, and the raison d'être behind it all. As Pepsi reflec
 ts in the film\, "The highest form of happiness is to make art."\nFree and
  open to the public.\nView the campus map for the theater location.\nFilm 
 Screening Timeline\n6–6:30 pm | Reception with the Artist\nEnjoy punch a
 nd cookies while you wait for the documentary to begin.\nEnter through The
  Studio's Visitor Entrance. Theater seating is unassigned.\n6:30–7:30 pm
  | Film Screening and Artist Interview\nWatch the documentary film Everlas
 ting in The Studio's Ackerman Family Theater. After the film\, The Studio'
 s Resident Advisor\, Bill Gudenrath\, will speak with Pepsi about the film
 . An audience Q&A will follow.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.t
 ime.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78466294/20261022180000
GEO:42.1498;77.0542
LOCATION:Corning Museum of Glass\, One Museum Way\, Corning\, NY\, 14830
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78466294/20261022180000
END:VEVENT
